        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en-Us",
            "description": "Collected all tweets from a 12-day period from when Harvey first formed until remnants left the U.S. Tweets were collected using Twitter API searching for keywords of wind and water threats that co-occurred in the same tweet. Search terms included the following:  ((tornado OR #tornado OR \\\"funnel cloud\\” OR funnelcloud) (\\\"flash flood\\” OR flood OR flashflood OR \\\"storm surge\\\" OR stormsurge)). Tweets were classified into three categories: public user (e.g. seeking information and sharing personal experience), authoritative user (e.g. sharing information but not personal information), or other (e.g. private or deleted accounts and bots). After classification, Twitter was re queried via the API to collect contextual tweet streams (entire user history) for the 12-day period for public and authoritative users. As January 2021, the dataset contains 131,754 tweets from 233 authoritative users and 208,725 tweets from 337 public users.",
            "descriptionType": "Abstract"
          }
        ],
